      "id": "evidence-003-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "`grep -x` on the whole line including the trailing `true`: an unanchored match would also accept the `false` rendering of the same sentence. The example's exit status is 0 either way, so a row checking only the command's exit code would pass on a negative result -- the failure mode this ledger keeps finding. Both streams are captured (`2>&1`) because a summary on stderr with `2>/dev/null` matches nothing and passes for the wrong reason.",
