    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY. It does not retire the 30 AxReal axioms and `nat_axiom_inventory` still reports `real: axiom=30`. `LraReconstructCtx::new` still builds the AxReal package and every shipped front-door LRA/SOS route still goes through it; this fact says the reconstruction NEED not, not that it does not. Making CReal the default carrier is a separate migration whose cost is the ~40 s `build_creal_prelude` (there is no `PreludeKey::CReal` in the prelude cache). Nor is a Lean MODULE on offer for the instantiated theorem: `render_lean_module` emits non-listed inductives as axioms, so a module for the closed False over CReal would emit the entire nat/int/rat/CReal development as axioms and defeat the claim. The load-bearing evidence here is the kernel's own `axiom_footprint`, not a rendered module.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
